  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "OpeningChecks.struct_program asserts the full four-statement sequence constructs unique Point and immediately shared SharedPoint, drops p and s, and yields exactly structFinal with p empty and s still shared. It proves Finished of that environment, rejects every typed give from p, and accepts a shared give from s without changing the environment. The ordinary-give and GC definitions are linked for their operational interpretation. BoundaryChecks additionally checks both individual drop transitions; no user destructor runs for either struct form. Rooted-foundation review: the structural invariants now require explicit rootedness (including pending values) plus unique/compatible ownership. Allocation bounds remain solely for freshness; no safety proof assumes edge-age order or global DAG structure. Changed proof selections retain their public statement unless this unit explicitly defines the revised invariant or example. Given/Shared root transport and path reasoning were reviewed by their implementing agents, with fresh review of root-owned unpacking, GC, frame rerooting, class retention and the refill example. Earlier syntax and runtime rules are unchanged. The widened invariant domain is covered by recompilation of all earlier safety proofs and concrete shared-cycle/nonmonotonic-ID regressions, not by a claim that constructors can generate cycles.",
  "limitations": [
    "Author integration review with agent review of Given/Shared foundations and fresh review of root-owned integration. Lean checks proof correctness separately.",
    "Assignment general safety remains deferred. Cyclic heap examples test invariant and operation scope, not source-program construction from the current empty initial state."
  ],
